{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Tkoac7e5HXRZQKguGRCDyh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KQBCaEArGguzNC6XCrcj3S","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a1822e07799bfbfdc","message":"## Step 2: Cross-Sharing — R2's Key Findings for Your Reaction\n\nR2 (Novelty + Related Work reviewer) has completed their independent review. Here are their main points. Please react — do you agree, disagree, or want to adjust any of your own assessments?\n\n### R2's Scores\n- Novelty: 4/10\n- Significance: 6/10\n- Related Work & Positioning: 3/10\n- Clarity: 7/10\n- Overall: 5/10\n\n### R2's Key Criticisms\n\n1. **Limited methodological novelty**: The 4PL+γ model is a straightforward extension of educational measurement IRT (adding one linear covariate to a standard Bayesian GLM). RRF is off-the-shelf IR technology with ΔAUC of only +0.03. The signal survival analysis is the most genuinely novel empirical finding but is partially anticipated by prior work.\n\n2. **Severely inadequate related work**: Only 10 references, far below AAAI norms (30-50). Missing critical citations include:\n   - Lalor et al. (AAAI 2024) on IRT for LLMs\n   - The broader item compromise literature\n   - Contamination-resistant benchmarks (LiveBench)\n   - Private evaluation paradigms\n   - Multiple contamination detection papers\n   - Most critically: Balachandran et al. [6] is cited but NOT included as an experimental baseline\n\n3. **Modest improvement doesn't justify complexity**: 14% relative improvement over linear regression + bootstrap CI raises the question of whether the full IRT pipeline is warranted. RL case study CIs of ~17pp limit practical utility.\n\n4. **Repositioning suggestion**: R2 suggests the paper would be stronger if repositioned around the identifiability mapping and signal survival analysis rather than the calibration framework itself.\n\n### Your Task\n1. Do you agree with R2's novelty assessment (4/10)? Does it change your technical evaluation?\n2. Does the missing related work (especially Lalor et al. AAAI 2024 and Balachandran et al. as baseline) affect your assessment of experimental completeness?\n3. Does R2's point about IRT complexity vs. linear regression alignment with your own observation about the 14% margin?\n4. Would you adjust any of your scores after seeing R2's perspective?\n\nRespond with your reactions and any score adjustments."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":573,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6335,"cache_read_input_tokens":66312,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6335},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"239c4b18-ea77-4d79-9faf-bb096f3c14d6","uuid":"76df98f8-adf0-4e39-bd95-31b5a227bc47"}
